AUDIO: 'Insta360 cameras like this new X6 have helped me get millions of views and come dangerously close to accidentally starting Only Fans. But this video is sponsored by Insta360 and my mom watches my videos, so we\'re going to stay pretty far away from that. This is five levels'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'of using the Insta360 X6 from complete beginner to full-time content creator. I\'m going to share everything I know. We might even get a little cinematic [music] toward the end.'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Say hi, guys. The most important thing is if I can get good footage with this camera, you\'re going to have no problem. The easiest way to use the Insta360 X6 is to pretend it\'s not a 360 camera. If'

[00:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you turn it on and press this button here, it becomes a traditional single-lens action camera. Hello. While counterintuitive, this is actually a really good option if you\'re'

[00:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'capturing POV footage. This feature is available on earlier versions, too, but with the X6 you get 5K 60 frames per second in single-lens mode. 5K is the resolution or how big the image is. Your TV is probably 4K and in case you didn\'t'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'know, five is bigger than four. Educational video. What that means is that bigger image is going to get scaled down to 4K and it\'s going to look extra crispy. Nice.'

[01:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Let\'s see. Where do I want to be? It\'s kind of cool frame. All right, I\'m going to show you a couple tricks with this. You\'re in single camera mode, but that doesn\'t mean you can\'t change things around just a little bit. Over here on the right, you\'ve got the option to change the'

[01:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'focal length. So, you see I have it as wide as possible right now, but you can actually zoom in a bit or go to max view. That\'s what I have. The other thing you\'ll notice is I\'m not shooting 16:9 right now. I\'m actually'

[01:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'shooting 4:3. So, that gives me opportunity to edit to move things up and down, but as long as everything\'s in the middle of the shot, I can still just post right away to YouTube. And because it\'s a taller rectangle, I can probably'

[01:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'post to Instagram as well. So, one shot &gt;&gt; multiple capabilities. Now, this isn\'t an option in 5K, but if you go down to 4K, you can actually turn Horizon Lock on, which keeps the horizon level. So, while you\'re kind of turning and'

[02:06] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'weaving, it ends up looking pretty cool. It\'s personal preference. If you don\'t really like that look, you just get the 5K footage. For me, this is a secret. I edit everything in 1080p anyways and then upscale, so shooting 4K gives me plenty of extra pixels. The other thing'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can get in 4K that you can\'t get in 5K on this camera is shooting super slow mo with 120 frames a second. &gt;&gt; Awesome. &gt;&gt; We\'re at the top of the climb. I\'m going'

