[03:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this climb and descent such a awesome thing to have in the middle of the city. I\'m on Horizon Lock. Horizon\'s not 100% locked in, but it kind of locks it, so you can see me swing my bike left to right. That\'s one thing to note. The other thing to note is you\'re locked'

[03:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'into a couple different frame rates. So, you can shoot 25 frames a second, 30 frames a second, 50 frames a second, and 60 frames a second. If you go to 4K, you can go up to 120 frames a second. Film is shot on 24 frames a second, and that'

[03:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is not an option. So, if you\'re one of those influencer YouTubers like me that likes to pretend they\'re shooting on film, you\'re not going to be able to do 24 frames a second in this mode, but you can do it in most of the other modes'

[03:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'including the 360 mode. If you\'re new to filming content online, I wouldn\'t worry about it too much. Most of the internet is actually shot at 30 frames a second. If you shoot at 60 frames a second and play that back at half speed at 30'

